  "description": "AHAGAS crystallizes in the orthorhombic crystal system with space group P n n a. Reported CIF formula moiety: C16 H68 Cl2 Gd6 N16 O23 6+,6(Cl1 1-),9(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd1B (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd2B (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd3B (Gd) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 15 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.514-5.167 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 87.97-179.17°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Gd6(μ6-O)(μ3-OH)8Cl2(L)4(H2O)14]Cl6·9H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 μ6-O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 8 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 14 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 μ6-O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 8 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 14 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
